<Project>

  <!-- The WebView2 package references its WPF control on every .NET 5+ target, with no
       switch to turn that off, and the WPF assembly asks for a WindowsBase that a
       WinForms app does not have: MSB3277, which -warnaserror makes a build failure.
       Dropped before references resolve rather than answered with UseWPF, which would
       bring the whole WPF framework into an app that has no WPF in it.

       Here rather than in Flux.App, because the package's build logic is transitive:
       every project that references the app inherits the same reference and the same
       failure, starting with its tests. A project without the package has nothing to
       remove, so this does nothing there. -->
  <Target Name="DropWebView2Wpf" BeforeTargets="ResolveAssemblyReferences">
    <ItemGroup>
      <Reference Remove="@(Reference)" Condition="'%(Filename)' == 'Microsoft.Web.WebView2.Wpf'" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
